Held back: IDE0049: this .NET SDK's 'dotnet format' ignores the suppressor StyleBro's multi-target guard uses for IDE rules, so their fixes could write C# or APIs that another target framework or project compiling the same file doesn't have. They aren't applied here; a newer .NET SDK's 'dotnet format' applies them where the guard allows.
Multi-targeted: one 'dotnet format' run per target framework (net10.0, net451, net48, net6.0, net7.0, netstandard2.0). net5.0, net8.0, net9.0, netcoreapp2.1, netcoreapp3.1: no run of their own, the code compiles the same as for another framework of the same kind (the same '#if' symbols tested, files and settings). net10.0, net7.0: only the projects whose code compiles differently there.
Shared files: these projects compile the same files with other '#if' symbols or settings, so each group gets a run of its own (loaded together, 'dotnet format' crashes: https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn/issues/86001): NetEscapades.EnumGenerators.IntegrationTests | NetEscapades.EnumGenerators.NetStandard.IntegrationTests | NetEscapades.EnumGenerators.NetStandard.SystemMemory.IntegrationTests | NetEscapades.EnumGenerators.PrivateAssets.IntegrationTests | NetEscapades.EnumGenerators.Tests; NetEscapades.EnumGenerators.IntegrationTests, NetEscapades.EnumGenerators.Interceptors.IntegrationTests | NetEscapades.EnumGenerators.NetStandard.IntegrationTests | NetEscapades.EnumGenerators.NetStandard.Interceptors.IntegrationTests | NetEscapades.EnumGenerators.NetStandard.SystemMemory.IntegrationTests | NetEscapades.EnumGenerators.PrivateAssets.IntegrationTests; NetEscapades.EnumGenerators.IntegrationTests | NetEscapades.EnumGenerators.PrivateAssets.IntegrationTests; NetEscapades.EnumGenerators.Generators, NetEscapades.EnumGenerators.Interceptors, NetEscapades.EnumGenerators.NetStandard.SystemMemory | NetEscapades.EnumGenerators.NetStandard.
